# L §5.19 (round 16, the fresh critic's settlement): "Every observation is booked on its own day", each end at a place
# no version covers "booked from the observation itself" (E §6.1 Booking observations); and "on any day, an instance
# that an observation the cut sees fulfils is never booked or measured, and its observations stand in for it" (E §4.1
# step 3). konto, covered by no version, opens at 100.00 PLN; fee_out takes 4.00 PLN each month from January to June
# (24.00 PLN), and in July its instance is fulfilled by the observed 5.00 PLN, booked on 2026-07-07 in its stead:
# 71.00 PLN at the end of July, flows of konto in July -5.00 PLN (q2); flows of fee_out: July 5.00 PLN, August 4.00 PLN
# (q).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source own "own"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input bank: observed
input dom: int
input fee_amt[y in years]: money PLN question "fee?"
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
move fee_out[m in months]: transfers
  on day_of(m, dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to world amount fee_amt[year_of(m)]
ask q: flows(fee_out, 2026-07), flows(fee_out, 2026-08)
ask q2: bal(konto, 2026-07-31), flows(konto, 2026-07)
version v
  cite own
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  dom = 7 "own"
  fee_amt[2026] = 4.00 PLN "own"
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "o"
version b
  cite own
  known 2026-07-08
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-07-07, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 5.00 PLN, fulfils: fee_out[2026-07]) "x"
=== expect
q: (5.00 PLN, 4.00 PLN)
  unfulfilled: fee_out[2026-08]
  cut 2026-10-20
q2: (71.00 PLN, -5.00 PLN)
  unfulfilled: fee_out[2026-01]
  unfulfilled: fee_out[2026-02]
  unfulfilled: fee_out[2026-03]
  unfulfilled: fee_out[2026-04]
  unfulfilled: fee_out[2026-05]
  unfulfilled: fee_out[2026-06]
  cut 2026-10-20
